/T (introduction The deciduous teeth start erupting at the age of 6.5 months \(mandibular central incisor\), and they finish at the age of 20-30 months. They are 20 in number while the permanent teeth are 32 in number. They are smaller in all dimensions and show less morphological variations than permanent teeth .)
/E (introduction The deciduous teeth start erupting at the age of 6.5 months \(mandibular central incisor\), and they finish at the age of 20-30 months. They are 20 in number while the permanent teeth are 32 in number. They are smaller in all dimensions and show less morphological variations than permanent teeth .)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
